ach layer become increasingly dissimilar. Similar to the sparsity in activations, in Appendix, we show that having different dropout \u03c1 for each layer (with lower \u03c1 for earlier layers to encourage resuability and higher \u03c1 for later layers to reduce interference between task-representations) can further improve the performance. Heterogeneous dropout provides a simple mechanism for balancing the reusability and interference of features depending on the similarity of tasks."
